3. Public Hosting Restriction

You may not Publicly Host the Software or a derivative work while it retains
the Protected Design or has a substantially similar overall visual
appearance.

Public Hosting is permitted if the Protected Design has first been replaced
with an independently created visual design that is not substantially
similar to the original. Merely changing the project name, text, branding,
or a few colors is not sufficient when the overall visual appearance remains
substantially similar.

